NSE LOG BOOK Undated · 2,688 Entries · Schedule C Categories · Quarterly Summaries Start in any month of any year","2":"THIS BOOK BELONGS TO Name Business name Phone Email EIN / Tax ID Accountant / tax preparer If found, please return to","3":"HOW TO USE THIS BOOK Undated by design Write the month at the top of any page and start. Begin in March, in July, in any year — nothing here expires when the year turns. One line per transaction Date, what it was, its category code, the amount in or out, whether it is deductible, and the running balance. The rows are wide on purpose: you can write in them with a real pen, not a fine liner. Categories are already printed The eighteen expense categories on the next page follow the lines of IRS Schedule C. Write the t","4":"EXPENSE CATEGORIES following IRS Schedule C Write the three-letter code in the Category column of the ledger. These follow the expense lines of Schedule C, so the totals transfer straight onto the form. ADV Advertising CAR Car & truck COM Commissions & fees CON Contract labour DEP Depreciation INS Insurance INT Interest LEG Legal & professional OFF Office expense RNT Rent or lease REP Repairs & maintenance SUP Supplies TAX Taxes & licences TRV Travel MEA Meals UTL Utilities WAG Wages OTH Other expenses YOUR OWN CAT","5":"THE YEAR AT A GLANCE Year Carry each month’s totals up here as you close it. One page, the whole year. MONTH INCOME EXPENSES NET NOTES January February March April May June July August September October November December YEAR WHAT CHANGED THIS YEAR · WHAT TO WATCH NEXT YEAR","6":"LEDGER Month Year DATE DESCRIPTION CATEGORY INCOME EXPENSE DED. BALANCE CARRIED FORWARD 1","7":"LEDGER Month Year DATE DESCRIPTION CATEGORY INCOME EXPENSE DED. BALANCE CARRIED FORWARD 2"},"start":4,"hero":["#36454a","#283336","#171d1f","rgba(134,162,182,.30)"],"spine":[0.5,0.55,0.57]}